Scope: this executes production `TargetWorkerOrdinaryDrr.runOrdinary` through its pure `Reads` seam with one Shard and synthetic in-memory queue heads. `N_backlog` is a synthetic remaining-Claim count; only each Target's current head is materialized. `payload_bytes` changes the synthetic scheduling cost but does not allocate or read a payload. Refresh/probe counters are seam calls, not persistent Store operations. The measurement excludes inventory construction and includes in-memory head replacement inside the timed Claim loop. It does not measure persisted read/write counts or bytes, Native work, multiple Shards, Profiles, quota work, bad-target progress, due lag, or Broker end-to-end behavior. These results are component-only; they make no before/after performance claim and do not close D3.

Validation:
